{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n\ndef is_good(f, p, k):\n    return all(f[(k * i) % p] == (k * f[i]) % p for i in range(p))\n\ndef gen(f, p, k, i):\n    if i == p:\n        return is_good(f, p, k)\n    return sum(gen(f + [j], p, k, i + 1) for j in range(p))\n\ndef solve(p, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    num_cycles = 0\n    seen = set()\n    for start in range(p):\n        if start not in seen:\n            num_cycles += 1\n            cur = start\n            while cur not in seen:\n                seen.add(cur)\n                cur = (cur * k) % p\n    power = num_cycles - (0 if k == 1 else 1)\n    return pow(p, power, MOD)\n\np, k = map(int, input().split())\nprint(solve(p, k))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long solve(long long p, long long k) {\n    const long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n    long long num_cycles = 0;\n    set<long long> seen;\n    \n    for (long long start = 0; start < p; start++) {\n        if (seen.find(start) == seen.end()) {\n            num_cycles++;\n            long long cur = start;\n            while (seen.find(cur) == seen.end()) {\n                seen.insert(cur);\n                cur = (cur * k) % p;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    long long power = num_cycles - (k == 1 ? 0 : 1);\n    \n    // Fast exponentiation modulo MOD\n    long long result = 1;\n    long long base = p % MOD;\n    while (power > 0) {\n        if (power & 1) {\n            result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        }\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        power /= 2;\n    }\n    \n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    cout << solve(p, k) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.271502545336261e-05, -5.602820692729438e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -7.748573807475623e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.597391747054644e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.043264344334602356, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.39069873094558716, -0.029750995337963104, -0.07891431450843811, -1.0013530300057027e-05, -0.0004379982128739357, -0.11282618343830109, -0.4757556915283203, -5.352353764465079e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0036396230570971966, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -0.33534446358680725, -0.22629372775554657, -6.318072337307967e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -3.2186455882765586e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.004626997280865908, -0.00015007323236204684, -3.814689989667386e-06, -3.3378546504536644e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00010907054820563644, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.861018856492592e-06, -0.3870564103126526, -7.390948667307384e-06, -0.16022898256778717, -0.03202556073665619, -3.099436753473128e-06, -3.576278118089249e